Falsifies `designware_mobile_storage::proofs::an_embedded_multimedia_card_bus_widens_only_after_the_card_took_the_switch`.

The defect: the status after `CMD6` is not checked for the switch error bit, so a card that
refused the width change still has the controller widened to meet it.

Expected to fail: the assertion in `SwitchWatchingWindowAndClock::write` that the controller's
bus widened only after the card took the switch.
diff --git a/src/sd.rs b/src/sd.rs
--- a/src/sd.rs
+++ b/src/sd.rs
@@ -551,9 +551,6 @@ pub(crate) fn switch<R: RegisterWindowAndClock, D: DirectMemoryAccessRegion>(
             status,
         ));
     }
-    if status & card::R1_SWITCH_ERROR != 0 {
-        return Err(MultimediaCardSwitchError::Refused(status));
-    }
     if card::r1_state(status) != card::R1_STATE_TRANSFER {
         return Err(MultimediaCardSwitchError::Unsettled(status));
     }
